{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 — RED -> GREEN, mutation-checked, held-out oracle. Gerrit 1995.\n\n### RED (oracle written BEFORE the fix, verified failing for the right reason)\n\nAdded 8 cases to `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_claim_transition_parent_cascade.py`\n(a `reactivation (closed -> in_progress)` section mirroring the existing reopen section)\nand 1 to `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py`. Against unpatched code,\n**5 failed and 4 passed trivially** (the no-op / cascade=False / wrong-current-status\ncases, which the missing edge does not affect):\n\n```\nFAILED test_reactivate_child_reactivates_closed_parent          - assert 'closed' == 'in_progress'\nFAILED test_reactivate_cascades_through_multiple_closed_levels  - 079d-... not cascaded\nFAILED test_reactivate_parent_failure_aborts_child_...          - DID NOT RAISE ConcurrencyError\nFAILED test_cli_reactivate_cascade_smoke                        - assert 'closed' == 'in_progress'\nFAILED test_reactivation_cascade_parent_gate_blocks_...         - DID NOT RAISE RebarError\n```\n\nEach fails through the proven mechanism, not the symptom: the gate case fails\n`DID NOT RAISE` precisely because with no cascade the parent's gate is never consulted.\n\nOne RED had to be re-designed: the gate test first tried to `review-plan` the closed\nchild, which fast-fails on a non-claimable ticket, so the assertion failed for the WRONG\nreason (unsigned attestation, not the cascade). Rebuilt with a gate-EXEMPT `bug` child so\nthe only possible source of the block is the cascaded parent. That is the \"fails for the\nright reason\" check doing its job.\n\n### Held out from the fixer\n\nThe oracle was moved OUT of the fix subagent's tree before it started (not merely omitted\nfrom its prompt) and both test paths were declared off-limits. The fixer got the\nmechanism, the reproduction, and a frozen contract card — never the fixture, assertions,\nor paths. It self-verified against its own throwaway scratch script.\n\n### GREEN + mutation\n\nOracle re-applied after the fixer finished: **122 passed** in the two files, green against\nan oracle it never saw. Mutation check (re-introducing the exact root cause — deleting the\n`(\"closed\", \"in_progress\"): \"closed\"` key — and rerunning): **the same 5 return to RED**,\nthen restored. The tests have teeth. Refactoring litmus: every assertion is on observable\nstate (`show_ticket()[\"status\"]`, exit codes, error text), never a private name or a source\ngrep, so a behaviour-preserving rename would not redden them.\n\n### The fix\n\nOne dict key in `_CASCADING_EDGES`. Everything else in the diff is prose the key makes\nfalse: the `transition` usage string, four docstrings, `docs/concurrency.md` I4a (third\ntable row + the gate-interaction note), and `docs/ticket-model.md` — the last of which was\n**already false before this change**, since it still claimed only `open -> in_progress`\ncascades, three months after the reopen edge landed.\n\nNo new helper, flag, code path, or dependency. No pre-existing test touched (the test diff\nis purely additive — zero deleted assertions).\n\n### Caller-dependency sweep\n\n`grep` for `closed -> in_progress` call sites across `src tests scripts docs` returns\n**nothing** but the reproduction itself — no caller depends on the non-cascading\nbehaviour. The `cascade=False` replay seam is unaffected and pinned by a new test. MCP\n`transition_ticket` delegates to `rebar.transition`, so it inherits the fix with no edit.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` PASS; `make typecheck` Success (616 files); complexity ratchet\n`active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`; `tests/interfaces` **1967 passed, 10 skipped,\n1 xfailed**. The `tests/unit` sweep is re-running: the first attempt died at 96% with\nexit 144 (SIGURG) after a local socket-server exception, with **zero** F/E markers and no\nFAILED/ERROR lines — an aborted process, not a test failure. Recorded rather than\nretried-until-green; the rerun result will be posted here.\n\n### Replication of the original report\n\nFresh store, real CLI, no library shortcuts:\n\n```\n$ rebar transition <child> closed in_progress\ntransitioned 8074-...: closed -> in_progress\nparent in_progress\nchild in_progress\n```\n\nPreviously `parent closed`. The reported invalid state no longer reproduces.\n\n### Landed for review\n\nGerrit **1995**: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1995 (commit 1ecd925393).\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787312504760451001,"uuid":"c92d5379-d6a0-4dd9-8a15-ed3e246ef84f"}